# SHRIMPING (HIP ESCAPE)

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Shrimping, also known as the Hip Escape, is a foundational ground movement designed to create space, recover position and improve movement efficiency while fighting from the ground.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the most important locomotion skills for grappling and self-defense.

---

# Philosophy

Ground fighting is movement before it is technique.

The athlete who can efficiently move the hips controls distance, escapes pressure and creates offensive opportunities.

CAS selects Shrimping whenever improving ground mobility and positional recovery is a priority.

